# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64073> (exendin-4)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64073> "A bioactive polypeptide of 39 amino acid residues isolated from the saliva of the Gila monster (<em>Heloderma suspectum</em>). High-affinity glucagon-like peptide 1 (GLP-1) receptor agonist (<em>K</em><small><sub>d</sub></small> = 136 pM); potently induces cAMP formation without stimulating amylase release in pancreatic acini; potentiates glucose-induced insulin secretion in isolated rat islets; protects against glutamate-induced neurotoxicity. A synthetic version is called exenatide.")
