# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64089> (vanoxerine)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64089> "An <em>N</em>-alkylpiperazine that consists of piperazine bearing 2-bis(4-fluorophenyl)methoxy]ethyl and 3-phenylpropyl groups at positions 1 and 4 respectively. Potent, competitive inhibitor of dopamine uptake (Ki = 1 nM for inhibition of striatal dopamine uptake). Has > 100-fold lower affinity for the noradrenalin and 5-HT uptake carriers. Also a potent sigma ligand (IC<small><sub>50</sub></small> = 48 nM). Centrally active following systemic administration.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "cas") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64089> "cas:67469-69-6")
