AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64101> "A benzamide obtained by formal condensation of the carboxy group of 4-fluorobenzoic acid with the primary amino group of 2-[4-(7-methoxynaphthalen-1-yl)piperazin-1-yl]ethylamine. Highly potent selective 5-HT<small><sub>1A</sub></small> receptor full agonist (pKi values are 9.0, 6.6, 7.5, 6.6 and < 6.0 for 5-HT<small><sub>1A</sub></small>, 5-HT<small><sub>1B</sub></small>, 5-HT<small><sub>1C</sub></small>, 5-HT<small><sub>2</sub></small> and 5-HT<small><sub>3</sub></small> receptors respectively). Possibly binds between the agonist binding site and the G protein interaction switch site, affecting the activation mechanism, and may display positive cooperativity. Anxiolytic following central administration in vivo.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "lincs.smallmolecule") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64101> "lincs.smallmolecule:LSM-3034")
