# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64114> (GR 127935)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64114> "A member of the class of  benzamides obtained by formal condensation of the carboxy group of 2'-methyl-4'-(5-methyl-1,2,4-oxadiazol-3-yl)biphenyl-4-carboxylic acid and the anilino group of 4-methoxy-3-(4-methylpiperazin-1-yl)aniline. Potent and selective 5-HT<small><sub>1B/1D</sub></small> receptor antagonist (pKi values are 8.5 for both guinea pig 5-HT<small><sub>1D</sub></small> and rat 5-HT<small><sub>1B</sub></small> receptors). Displays > 100-fold selectivity over 5HT<small><sub>1A</sub></small>, 5-HT<small><sub>2A</sub></small>, 5-HT<small><sub>2C</sub></small> receptors and other receptor types. Centrally active following oral administration.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "cas") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64114> "cas:148672-13-3")
