AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64156> "An imidothiocarbamic ester that consists of isothiourea in which the thiol hydrogen is substituted by a 2-(imidazol-4-yl)ethyl group. An extremely potent, high affinity agonist at H<small><sub>3</sub></small> and H<small><sub>4</sub></small> receptors (Ki values are 0.3 and 2.7 nM respectively). Induces shape change in eosinophils with an EC<small><sub>50</sub></small> of 25 nM. Centrally active following systemic administration.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "cas") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_64156> "cas:102203-18-9")
